        "recommend_reason_data": "<h3 class=\"section-title text-center mt20 mb-lg-5 mb-4\">Why are we recommending these?</h3>\n<div class=\"why-recommending-row text-center item\"><h5 class='symbol counter-highlight'>1</h5><p class=\"this-mean vr-block-ele\"><strong>Because of your long investment horizon</strong></p><p class=\"this-mean mt-1 mb10\">We’re suggesting investing in a combination of equity and debt funds, given your moderate risk profile</p><p class=\"this-mean grey-text mb0\">Invest 75% of your money in the provided equity funds. The latter will provide geographical diversification so that a sharp correction in the Indian markets will not affect your entire investment. Invest the balance 25% in the provided Short Duration fund. This portfolio can earn higher returns than the rate of inflation as well as fixed-income investment options. But there will be ups and downs along the way.</p><p class=\"this-mean grey-text mb0\">You should rebalance these investments periodically to keep the equity allocation between 65% and 85% of the total portfolio value. For example, if the equity allocation rises above 85%, you should sell some of the equity fund holding and invest it in the provided debt fund(s) to restore it to 75%.</p></div>\n<div class=\"why-recommending-row text-center item\"><h5 class='symbol counter-highlight'>2</h5><p class=\"p--section-desc p--section-desc-16px vr-block-ele\"><strong>Because you’ve chosen to invest a lumpsum amount</strong></p><p class=\"this-mean grey-text mb10 mt10\">It is better not to invest all your money at one go in equity funds. Spread the equity portion of your lumpsum amount over a number of months as per the provided investment plan.</p></div>\n<input type='hidden' id='counter-type' value='2'>"
